From: Ivo Nunes <ivo@nunes.uk>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:14:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Read DirectInput controllers in shared mode

Godot reads joypads through SDL, whose DirectInput backend opens each
controller in exclusive mode so it can play SDL's own rumble effects.
DirectInput lets only one holder have exclusive access, so Purr's
force feedback module (WheelForceFeedback), which needs it to play
forces on a steering wheel, couldn't take a wheel that Godot was
already reading as a joypad.

SDL now opens DirectInput controllers in shared mode. Axes, buttons
and hats read the same; Input.start_joy_vibration no longer reaches
DirectInput-only devices (XInput, Windows.Gaming.Input and HIDAPI
controllers, which most gamepads are, are unaffected).

Test: on Windows, with a DirectInput force feedback wheel connected,
samples/force_feedback opens the wheel and plays a force while the
wheel's axes keep moving in Input.

Not for upstream: Godot has no force feedback of its own that needs it.
---
 godot/thirdparty/sdl/joystick/windows/SDL_dinputjoystick.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/godot/thirdparty/sdl/joystick/windows/SDL_dinputjoystick.c b/godot/thirdparty/sdl/joystick/windows/SDL_dinputjoystick.c
index c6712600..c68b1986 100644
--- a/godot/thirdparty/sdl/joystick/windows/SDL_dinputjoystick.c
+++ b/godot/thirdparty/sdl/joystick/windows/SDL_dinputjoystick.c
@@ -789,10 +789,11 @@ bool SDL_DINPUT_JoystickOpen(SDL_Joystick *joystick, JoyStick_DeviceData *joysti
     }
 
     /* Acquire shared access. Exclusive access is required for forces,
-     * though. */
+     * though. Purr: shared, so Purr's force feedback (which needs
+     * exclusive access) can take wheels while they're read here. */
     result =
         IDirectInputDevice8_SetCooperativeLevel(joystick->hwdata->InputDevice, SDL_HelperWindow,
-                                                DISCL_EXCLUSIVE |
+                                                DISCL_NONEXCLUSIVE |
                                                     DISCL_BACKGROUND);
     if (FAILED(result)) {
         return SetDIerror("IDirectInputDevice8::SetCooperativeLevel", result);
